  "body": "My issues that was caused by the element are the following:\r\n\r\n- You can't style the base characters without the markup.\r\n- When you want the family name and the given name to separate, current implementation goes wild.\r\n\r\nPlease see the codepen below. (Japanese, because of ruby)\r\nhttps://codepen.io/NagayamaToshiaki/pen/gOXLJxZ\r\n\r\nIn the example above, I consider the second <rt> should be over 角栄, but カクエイ is above \"_角栄\" including spacebar.\r\n\r\nThe space issue might be the bug of Chrome, but let me start discussion.",
